          "createdAt": "2025-06-18T08:14:43Z",
          "updatedAt": "2025-06-18T08:14:43Z",
          "comments": [
            {
              "originalPosition": 44,
              "body": "For \"policy\", I think of a document, or at least an intentional decision. But it could be that one doesn't support it because the software doesn't support it (as is the case for deSEC).\r\n\r\n(The software really does, but we've not made a serious attempt to connect one of our public-facing nameservers with our authentication system. Perhaps you'd say this is policy, but I don't feel that's the right term. It's rather \"not implemented\".)\r\n\r\nAgain, not feeling strongly. -- We could say \"for a number of reasons\" instead of \"policy and other\". Wdyt?",
              "createdAt": "2025-06-18T08:14:43Z",
              "updatedAt": "2025-06-18T08:14:43Z"
            }
          ]
        },
